{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.corrected_markov_trace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.corrected_markov_trace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Algebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":1,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.corrected_markov_trace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.corrected_markov_trace","kind":"theorem","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/ParticleInteractions/corrected_markov_trace.lean#L24-L42","doc":"**Markov trace of `σ₀σ₁σ₀`.** Let `tr : A → R` be `R`-linear, cyclic,\nwith `tr 1 = 1` and `tr σ₀ = z`, let `σ₀² = h•σ₀ + 1` (Hecke relation),\nand let the Markov property hold for the word `σ₀² σ₁` (here `σ₀² ∈ H₂`\nand `σ₁` is the maximal generator). Then `tr(σ₀σ₁σ₀) = h·z² + z`.\n\nProof: cyclicity gives `tr(σ₀σ₁σ₀) = tr(σ₀²σ₁)`; Markov gives\n`z · tr(σ₀²)`; Hecke and linearity give `z · (h·z + 1)`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:corrected-markov-trace","label":"prop:corrected-markov-trace","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/corrected-markov-trace.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}